# arc-ready (Cursor adaptation)
#
# Cursor has no Agent Skills loader. This file points it at the skill body,
# which is self-contained: nothing else loads by default.

When the user asks to take a software project from idea to launch, or for any one
stage of it (write a PRD, design the architecture, sequence a roadmap, choose a stack,
scaffold a repo, build a slice, deploy with rollback, add SLOs and alerts, prepare a
launch, or run an OWASP or compliance review), read `arc-ready/SKILL.md` and follow it.

Run `bash arc-ready/scripts/arc-check.sh status` at the start of every turn. It checks
the progress ledger in `.arc-ready/PROGRESS.md` against disk and names the next tier.
Record transitions with `arc-check.sh mark <tier> <status>`; `done` is refused until the
tier gate passes. Immediately before any public release, run `arc-check.sh prepublish`
and never publish on a block.

Artifacts live at stable `.<tier>-ready/` paths (`.prd-ready/PRD.md`,
`.architecture-ready/ARCH.md`, and so on). Write only evidence you actually produced.
